This error is reproducible and occurs with the latest changes <https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/commit/f2b16c414f35d1bfd6229587f4d98ec76c0d5759> to shiny.

Running the example of observeEvent() or eventFilter() gives the following error:

Error in handler(binary, message) :
  No handler registered for for type saveButton:actionButton

That said, all previous shiny apps utilising actionButton() in "legacy mode" (i.e. as in the example of actionButton()) return the same error and stop working as soon as a button is pressed.

Example of observeEvent()
## Not run:
# In ui.R:
shinyUI(basicPage(
  numericInput("n", "Number of observations", 5),
  actionButton("saveButton", "Save")
))
# In server.R:
shinyServer(function(input, output) {
  observeEvent(input$saveButton, function() {
    write.csv(runif(input$n), file = "data.csv")
  })
})

## End(Not run)

