From uea11a7a12a3e1e0b at groups.google.com  Tue Oct 14 13:07:32 2014
From: uea11a7a12a3e1e0b at groups.google.com (Julia Thorpe)
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2014 13:07:32 +0000
Subject: How to prevent "error: cannot open the connection" when users try to upload data?
Message-ID: <eb1A_7AhGBE.6qFpd1veV3EJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shinyapps-users/c/eb1A_7AhGBE/m/6qFpd1veV3EJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I have created a shiny app where users can upload .csv files and then apply some network analysis methods to the data.

The problem I am having is that when the user tries to upload a file, the error "Error: cannot open the connection" appears. This does not happen when I run the app locally, and it does not happen when the user selects one of the demo files that I have included in the app.

The way I have allowed users to upload data is with the line:

> read.csv(file.choose(),header=TRUE,check.names=FALSE)

or in another case:

> read.csv(file.choose(),header=TRUE,row.names=1,check.names=FALSE)

I am not sure how to get around this issue, and would appreciate any help at all!

Best regards,
Julia

From uedbcc711cdbb3da8 at groups.google.com  Tue Oct 14 13:46:21 2014
From: uedbcc711cdbb3da8 at groups.google.com (Tareef Kawaf)
